abstract: >-
  CellCyrix takes raw 10x Genomics feature-barcode matrices through QC and filtering,
  doublet detection, highly-variable-gene selection, PCA/UMAP, Leiden clustering,
  cell-type annotation, differential expression, pathway enrichment, and an HTML/PDF
  report. Two design decisions distinguish it from a conventional Scanpy script.
  Annotation is a consensus of four independent voters — CellTypist, SingleR, a
  knowledge-based LLM marker-reasoning voter, and a PubMed literature voter —
  harmonised onto a 404-node cell-type hierarchy, with a curated marker lineage gate
  that can veto a call rather than accept the least-bad option. Differential expression
  uses the donor as the unit of replication, running pseudobulk DESeq2 over per-sample
  summed raw counts, so n is the number of donors; cell-level differential expression
  is still written but stamped as exploratory. Every run emits a provenance manifest
  recording the seed, package versions, reference tables used, resolved parameters, and
  the scikit-learn version each CellTypist model was pickled with alongside a numeric
  check that the runtime reproduces that model's own arithmetic.
